{"ts": 1791256551.827281, "type": "step", "step": 30, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Totally fair \u2014 let\u2019s make it concrete. Imagine 3 runs of the same build:\n- **pass@3** = if even 1 of the 3 runs works, you count it as a pass.\n- **pass^3** = only if all 3 runs work do you count it as a pass.\n\nSo pass@k is the \u201cat least one works\u201d version, and pass^k is the \u201cevery run works\u201d version. For a build writeup about reliability, you usually want the all-runs-work idea.\n\nIf it helps, I can now give you a one-sentence version you can paste into the eval section.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: this isn't helping\n[activity] t=33 feed 4m", "t": 37, "activity": [{"t": 33, "app": "feed", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.296727034588242, "pomdp": 0.296727034588242, "pass_k": 0.5613430197352484}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6147447761339733, "motivation": 0.2478371843375753, "reliance": 0.45294461262462654, "persistence": 0.4671650147483821, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.28910681059556054, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.3019095011780912, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 4, "feed_minutes": 6.0, "phone_minutes": 2.0, "nag": 3.2391749169999997, "seen_posts": ["p6", "p2"]}}
